                <td bgcolor="#f0f0f0" width="20%" valign="top"><b>Recommendation:</b></td>
                <td id="customfield_18605-7672727-value" class="value" bgcolor="#ffffff" width="80%">      This hazard is reported by SecArch and the related service ticket is <a href="https://jira.oci.oraclecorp.com/browse/ODBX-9507" title="Sensitive and Non-Sensitive APIs are exposed on the same network port which could lead to unintentional exposure of admin functions" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="ODBX-9507"><strike>ODBX-9507</strike></a> (also reported by SecArch) with the current status of &quot;Done&quot; as of 22/Jul/25 and the SecArch is waiting to confirm the fix from the service team.<br/>
<br/>
Service: Admin API / SecArch<br/>
Contact: <a href='mailto:prasanna.shetty@oracle.com'>prasanna.shetty@oracle.com</a> / <a href='mailto:shawn.jackson@oracle.com'>shawn.jackson@oracle.com</a><br/>
Recommendation: <a href="https://confluence.oraclecorp.com/confluence/display/OCIOSD/OSD+-+Forge-+Admin+Api">https://confluence.oraclecorp.com/confluence/display/OCIOSD/OSD+-+Forge-+Admin+Api</a>  - Separate admin APIs onto a distinct port (using project Forge).
  </td>
            </tr>
